+#### Currency exposure cap
+
+If you trade several pairs that are all priced against, or settled in, the same underlying currency - for example a handful of BTC-settled futures, or several coins that are all quoted in the same stablecoin - a large adverse move in that one currency can hit several of your open trades at the same time, even though each trade looked fine in isolation.
+
+`max_currency_exposure` lets you cap this concentration risk. It's a ratio (between `0.0` and `1.0`) of your total tradable capital ([respecting `tradable_balance_ratio` / `available_capital`](#tradable-balance)) that may be committed, in total, to simultaneously open trades sharing the same quote/settlement currency.
+
+```json
+"max_currency_exposure": 0.5
+```
+
+With the above, no more than 50% of your tradable capital may be committed at once to open trades sharing a given quote currency. When opening (or adding to, via [position adjustments](strategy-callbacks.md#adjust-trade-position)) a trade would push the combined stake for that currency above the configured share, the stake amount is reduced to fit under the limit, or the trade is skipped entirely if no room is left. This is enforced identically in live/dry-run and in backtesting, the same way other entry-sizing adjustments are, and the reason is logged just like other stake-amount adjustments (e.g. "Stake amount for pair ... is too big").
+
+This setting can also be set in the strategy, see [Strategy Override](#parameters-in-the-strategy). By default, this cap is disabled.
+
 #### Amend last stake amount
 
 Assuming we have the tradable balance of 1000 USDT, `stake_amount=400`, and `max_open_trades=3`.
